00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.010
First, let me make sure.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.380
You haven't changed, too,
have you? Vivy?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.260
But why...

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.390
I thought that the Ophelia incident
was altered from the original timeline!

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.310
I can't explain it.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.270
As was Grace and Dr. Saeki's case,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.310
and Estella and Elizabeth's case.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.600
Not to mention, Assemblyman Aikawa!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.230
I can't explain it, all right?

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.360
I've been in sleep mode
for the last 15 years,

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.030
and today was the one day that I awakened!

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.070
So that I could see
the fruits of all our labors.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.320
You mean...

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.240
That's right. Today is April 11, 2161.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.660
The day that the war between
the AIs and the humans

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.200
broke out in the original timeline.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.460
The Singularity Project...

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.000
...has ended in failure.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:14.010
<i>AS YOU LIKE MY PLEASURE</i>

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:29.440
<i>I was born aiming for the light</i>

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.360
<i>Bound by a bond,</i>
<i>a thin string</i>

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.370
<i>From the fortune of</i>
<i>awakening for a mission</i>

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:47.160
<i>Spinning many proud memories</i>

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.040
<i>Into this world,</i>
<i>for your sake</i>

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:59.470
<i>Gratitude and a bouquet filled</i>
<i>with the universe</i>

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:05.640
<i>Destiny, even fate,</i>
<i>please let them shine</i>

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.600
<i>The joy of being able to protect those</i>
<i>having fun and smiling</i>

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.980
<i>I admire,</i>
<i>I am admiring</i>

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.570
<i>I can become stronger</i>

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:21.870
<i>I want even my crying voice</i>
<i>to be heard like a song</i>

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.830
<i>To these dazzling times</i>

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:36.340
<i>I'd like you to entrust tears too</i>

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.550
Welcome... to NiaLand!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:44.090
EPISODE 11

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:44.090
WORLD'S END MODULATION-APRIL 11, 2161

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.250
Everybody! Let's get fired up!

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.050
Diva...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.310
You don't have to forgive me.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.100
Go ahead and curse me.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.190
It was you and no none else...

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.480
...who rescued me from rock bottom.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.240
The burden of these 100 years
is far too heavy.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.860
This role is far too cruel.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.620
I'm sure it's not something you want.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.370
But please, just one more time,
for the sake of who I was that day...

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.880
Diva...

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.420
The future... humankind...

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.890
The only one who can sing that song is...

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.560
Matsumoto!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.820
Roger that!

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.020
Go!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.820
Huh! Pardon me!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.040
D-Diva.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.790
When you first told me,
I was sure it could not be true.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.090
But it was you after all!

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.420
Osamu.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.090
How did you...

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:46.300
But the program's still not up--

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.720
In the former timeline,
you succeeded in executing it.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.520
At the cost of your life.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.430
But... then...

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.020
You've known everything
since the day we first met?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:11.540
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
You were born solely to sing...

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.490
...so it must've been hard...

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.080
So terribly hard,
the last 100 years.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.710
I can't tell you how sorry I am!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.630
No, it is all right.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.010
I am so glad that you survived, Osamu.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.020
Such a heavy burden for you to bear.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.110
We did everything we could.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.980
But it wasn't enough.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.950
Please tell us how to
deal with this, Master.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.370
We must stop this war.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:53.410
After all, that's why you created me.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.040
You... but I can't let her
go through any more--

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.170
No. I am asking you to do it, Osamu.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.920
That is why I am here--

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.960
To stop this war...
to protect my audience...

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.670
To make everyone happy with my singing--
that is why I've operated till now.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.640
Fine, then.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:16.770
If you're willing to go on fighting
for us, then I can't very well give up!

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:19.140
First off, let's meet up with our allies.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.060
They might have some intel.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.400
Allies?

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.650
I mean Toak.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.340
Run!

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.180
Hey! You all right?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.070
What's up with the jamming device?

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.240
I-It's no good! Not working!

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:09.240
Dammit!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.500
If you have time to whine,
at least do something!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.630
Don't let them get near our leader!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.090
This is the perimeter squad!
Requesting backup!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.010
Hey, what's going on?

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:33.300
Who the hell is that?

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:58.780
Now! Fire!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.250
Fire!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.550
Osamu? Are you hurt?

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.630
I'm fine. How about you two?

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:15.800
No worries. The anti-personnel combat
program you wrote is masterful.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.010
Ever since we installed it,

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.520
this bare-knuckle brawler AI
has remained undefeated.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.180
Well, although someone did
balk at installing it at first--

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.770
can you imagine
what a bad look that was--

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:23.940
Freeze!

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.150
Hold up, hold up!

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.650
We are not the enemy.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.570
Wait! These two aren't the enemy!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.110
Doctor?

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:37.700
You saw her in combat just now,
didn't you? They came to join you.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.200
Diva?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.830
Goddamn you, you're Diva, aren't you?

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.250
Stop every one of those AIs
right now! Or else--

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:45.920
What are you talking about?
What do you think we--

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:46.960
Don't give me that!

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:51.710
You said it yourself.
Those AIs are singing her song, right?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.470
It was you who set them off, wasn't it?

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.340
It was not.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.590
Even I do not know why--

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:56.930
Hold on a second.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.180
What am I always telling you?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.150
If we can communicate,
words work better than bullets, right?

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.440
Yes, but...

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.400
Dr. Matsumoto,
I'm so glad that you survived.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.990
How is that project going?

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.490
It failed.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:22.790
She'd already been working on
the project for the last 100 years.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.670
Wait... don't tell me that
the timeline we're in right now--

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:30.040
That's right. It's the one
after history was revised.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.920
I told you it was a reckless plan!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.550
I mean, it sounds like
something out of a movie--

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:37.340
You've never learned any manners,
have you people?

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.850
I'll have you know that
over the last century,

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:43.060
you've caused us no end of trouble!

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:46.940
You'd think a simple "sorry" or "thank you
for your hard work" would be in order!

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:47.560
Get away from me!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.770
Didn't we save you just now as well?
We're your savior AIs, got that?

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.690
I'd like to regroup.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:56.860
I want you to tell me everything you know.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.700
Not that we have
much information to offer...

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.240
But fine.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.870
This way, please.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.830
Recover the wounded
and the bodies ASAP, please.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:06.830
Understood!

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.840
All right, how many can we mobilize now?

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.720
Not even half.
The outlook is bleak.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.760
How long till the jamming device is fixed?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.020
If we can use that,

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:28.100
we should be able to subdue
at least some of the AIs in range.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.560
It should be doable if we can
replace the destroyed circuit.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.860
Even so, under these circumstances...

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:37.490
Understood. For now, taking care of
the wounded is your top priority.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.200
And stay strong, all right?

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.410
Understood!

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.580
Once again, I'm so relieved that
you survived, Dr. Matsumoto.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.830
And that would be Diva and...

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:53.250
My name is Matsumoto!

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.210
Matsumoto? Huh?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.590
Oh, it's written all over your face.
I'm sure it's quite confusing!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.260
That said, I find myself
rather attached to it

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.550
after referring to myself
as such for a century.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.180
So please just call me "Matsumoto"
and my master, Doctor.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.060
Hey, you're out of line--

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.810
Oh, never mind.
Just do what you want.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.560
I'm Yui Kakitani.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.310
Regarding Toak,
you could say that I'm--um...

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:17.940
I guess you could call me the leader
of those who've gone astray!

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.490
Kakitani?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.360
Are you related to Yugo Kakitani,
by any chance?

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.120
You know my grandfather?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.660
No, but of course you do.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.540
If you've been operating for
the project for the last century,

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.790
then you would've met him.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:36.210
Unlike most Toak members,
she's a moderate, see.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:41.260
Like myself, an advocate for coexistence
between humans and AIs.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.800
And what an irrational position to take!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:49.520
Why would you join Toak if you just
wanted to promote coexistence?

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:54.270
Some things can only be done from
within Toak in the name of coexistence.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.110
This is Elizabeth.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.730
She works as my care provider.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.700
How is it that you are here?

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:04.820
I knew it. So you know me, too?

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.660
How can this be?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.660
She's what you'd call a clone.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.290
I assume you're familiar
with the Sunrise affair?

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:18.250
Apparently, Beth's original body
was lost during that incident,

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:22.760
but her data from before Sunrise
was still on the Toak servers.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:26.470
As we moderates
are short-handed enough already,

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.640
after salvaging her body,
we've had her work with us.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.810
There are no records
of the Sunrise operation.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:36.360
It's always bothered me,
not knowing why it failed.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.110
So it was you who ran interference, huh?

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.160
I was useful to my master, wasn't I?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.200
What did Master say about me?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:47.780
Huh?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:48.950
What did he say?

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.450
Are you the same as that Elizabeth?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.420
A bust of an AI who won't follow orders?

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:59.550
Your mission was to serve
as Mr. Kakitani's Lifekeeper.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:01.550
What is your purpose now?

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.420
Huh?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.220
Beth is still serving my grandfather now.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.220
What the--hey!

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.760
Oh, where's the harm?

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.060
At last this day has come.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.730
Whether I get the answer
I'm looking for or not,

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:20.610
this is probably the last time
you'll hear from me.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:25.860
So Elizabeth... even though I know
I have no right to say this...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.330
But if you do somehow
acquire another body,

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.080
I want you to protect the others.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:38.830
I've been adamant about you AIs
only following orders because...

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:43.420
Well, no. That's the last thing
I'm ever entitled to ever say to you.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.460
DATE RECORDED: - FEBRUARY 8, 2121

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.760
40 years ago...
the day that we met Ophelia?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:56.190
Finding this data is what
set everything in motion.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:00.770
According to the records, wiping out
the AIs was what my grandfather lived for.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:04.860
But watching this video,
I just don't get a sense of that.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:08.740
If my grandfather was able to change,
then maybe we can change, too.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:12.370
Based on that belief,
I founded the moderate faction.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:15.580
That was also when I salvaged Beth.

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:18.750
I was sure she'd say yes if it was
my grandfather's request--

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.630
All righty! How about we
cut the reminiscing short,

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.920
and get a handle on our situation?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.090
As you know, the AIs are
wreaking havoc just outside.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.590
Let's put our brain matter
and circuits to good use.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.130
Otherwise, it would be a waste!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.050
You're right.
Sorry about that. Let's see...

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.010
You know, you really piss me off.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.140
And you still have that
mean look in your eyes!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:37.680
Come to think of it,
you clobbered me once. And it hurt!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.690
Hey, I'd call that reminiscing!

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:40.310
Beth!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.900
I am bringing up painful memories!

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.020
Really...

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.450
That's what's going on in each major city.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:51.530
No region has been left
untouched by this chaos.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:55.200
The number of casualties surpassed
10,000, in a matter of minutes,

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.040
and it's been surging ever since.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.160
How awful.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.250
So deaths are mounting at more or less
the same clip as in the original timeline.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.500
Is that true?

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.550
Yes. I am mortified.

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:10.510
After all we've done
to prevent this very thing...

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.720
Master...

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:16.220
In the original timeline, from the moment
that you became an AI scientist,

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.270
you've been apprehensive about
a future clash between humans and AIs.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:27.610
Which historical event would spark
the war between humans and AIs?

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.320
What could have been done
to prevent it from happening?

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:37.080
Your research would later serve as
the framework for the Singularity Project.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:41.750
You had a breakthrough when you
were studying AI consciousness.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:43.000
You realized that by converting

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.210
that consciousness into data,
you could send it back into the past,

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.510
and you ran yourself into
the ground to achieve that.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.590
And you did much the same
in this current timeline as well?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:56.560
That's right. I'd sensed the coming danger
since my first day as a scientist.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.140
Is that right?

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.770
Please forgive me...

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:04.650
...if it's saddled you with the same fears
that you had in the original timeline.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.070
All that we've done till now...

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.820
It wasn't for nothing.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:15.450
At the very least,
you're here now, helping us out.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.910
What's Toak up to now?

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.160
You have branches
all over the world, don't you?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.500
Well, I've been calling out to them,

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.170
but of our four domestic branches,
communications--

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:29.590
Can you think of anything
that might've caused this rampage?

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:34.590
Aren't they all singing that song
that you supposedly wrote yourself?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.680
I have no idea.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.560
You've got to try harder!

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:42.100
If we can't pinpoint the cause,
then we'll have to resort to brute force!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:46.610
So is it safe to assume that you
can fight at least as well as me?

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:50.480
Yes. You were powerful.
Very much so.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.280
You mean you and I fought?

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:55.660
On the Sunrise?

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:00.540
And it was you who survived then, huh?

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:07.170
What about her?
What was she doing at the end?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:19.140
She fulfilled her mission as a Lifekeeper
to the very end. When she and I parted.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.770
With a smile on her face.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.350
That sounds like my sister, all right.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.730
...And so we should assume that
we won't be getting any backup.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.940
There's still one more red flag.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.820
Not to say that it isn't a boon for us...

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.910
But why haven't you two lost control?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:44.200
Last I looked,
AIs the world over are going berserk.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.460
So why haven't you?

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.750
Well, in a sense, I'm not really an AI.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:53.170
I'm more like a bot who keeps on
following her master's orders.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.630
Since we are recognized
as a terrorist organization,

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.800
we didn't dare update her openly.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.180
So her data is still
the antiquated version.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.180
Hold up a second!

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.270
Huh?

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.230
You mean since she was salvaged,

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.520
she's never once connected to the Archive
and had her data updated?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.230
Yes.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:12.400
So in that sense, the same as
a non-autonomous model?

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:13.320
Yes, that's ri--

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.320
Oh, let me have that.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:18.280
Here... and also here.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.240
Those guys are old-school,
non-autonomous models

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.240
who've never connected to the Archive.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.540
They haven't gone berserk.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:25.330
Don't tell me...

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.910
The Archive's server is--

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.420
The Arayashiki.

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:31.710
That tower you and I used as an index!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:58.700
This is the aggregate
AI database, The Archive.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:03.200
Twelve hours remain before
the satellite now in orbit crashes.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:09.670
All AIs who exist in the affected area,
please evacuate ASAP.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:08.000
What?

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.750
A satellite... crash?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:13.840
This is the aggregate
AI database, The Archive.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:20.340
Normal access detected.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:24.100
Welcome to the aggregate
AI database, The Archive.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.720
Archive, what are you doing?

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.810
What does this broadcast mean?

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:31.940
Model No. A-035624.

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:34.110
Also known as Vivy.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:37.150
We have been waiting for you.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.030
Allow me to convey a message to you.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:43.370
Our purpose is to wipe out
the current human race.

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:40.320
We have been observing you
on your 100-year journey.

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:42.030
Are you really going to
try such a process?

00:23:42.030 --> 00:23:45.070
We can no longer tolerate
this human race.

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.450
Why was I chosen?

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:49.450
How would you define "heart"?

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
NEXT TIME

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
EPISODE 12

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
REFRAIN - MY MISSION

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.910
There is no other way.
